{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1003615-path-hack-ideas","id":1003615,"title":"Path hack ideas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-15T14:45:04-08:00","id":1003615,"title":"Path hack ideas?","content":"I'm looking for some ideas on changing up the Paths a bit.<br /> <br /> Goal - 4 (or 5?) 'whole' paths, 1 'corrupted' path.<br /> <br /> Motivation - In addition to campaign-specific setting hack stuff (see below) I don't like the combination of Alchemists &amp; Necromancers in a single path, nor do I see Necromancy working well without Spirit (how else do you create undead than binding a spirit to a lifeless corpse!).<br /> <br /> <br /> My idea is to replace the Watchtowers w/ Cornerstones; the true foundations of reality. One of these was cracked when reality was shattered by the Exarchs (or in my game hack, probably by Technomancers rewriting history &amp; becoming/always having been the Exarchs), with part of it remaining in the Supernal while another portion resides in the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> This shattered Cornerstone is a forbidden path, as most mages who forge* a connection with it find their magic, and eventually their minds, corrupted by the broken nature of their magical anchor. Some find the temptation too great to resist, however; whether from a desire for greater power or the hubris of thinking they might be the one to heal the broken Cornerstone and in so doing reconnect the Fallen World and the Supernal.<br /> <br /> I've played around a bit w/ the Ascension to Awakening translation guide and the idea of using the translated Ascension thingies (forget what they were called - Questing, Dynamic, etc.) + 'Unity' or something like that. I do like the Aw division into different 'types' of mages, however - witches, warlocks, etc.<br /> <br /> Maybe the answer is to split Moros so that Alchemists stick with it, &amp; move Necromancers over to a broken 6th Cornerstone? If I did that, I could replace Death w/ something like Prime or Forces for the Alchemists, and replace Matter with Spirit for the new 6th path for Necromancers. Of course, that breaks the setting-wide '5 by 5' style symmetry, so I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> What are some path hacks others have tried?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12661-snapdragyn","name":"Snapdragyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T16:08:07-08:00","id":1003654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snapdragyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1003615-path-hack-ideas#post1003615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like the combination of Alchemists &amp; Necromancers in a single path, nor do I see Necromancy working well without Spirit (how else do you create undead than binding a spirit to a lifeless corpse!).<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>By binding a ghost of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T16:43:34-08:00","id":1003668,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/883338-the-other-five-paths-2e\">I'll just leave this here for inspiration.</a> In particular, consider using the \u201cAnother World\u201d option, where artisans, bargainers*, druids, sages, and sorcerers replace alchemists/necromancers, shamans, theurges, witches, and warlocks. The main reason why you might consider doing this is that it breaks up the alchemists and the necromancers, folding the alchemists in with the artisans and the necromancers in with the druids. <br /> <br /> * I really need a better name for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-17-2016, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T17:20:29-08:00","id":1003689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1003615-path-hack-ideas?p=1003654#post1003654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By binding a ghost of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>To elaborate: in Awakening, spirits and ghosts (and goetia, and Supernal entities, etc.) are not the same thing, despite being intangible entities. In particular, each involves a different Arcanum: Spirit for spirits, Death for ghosts, Mind for goetia, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweav